@startuml
!include ./nora-medlink-style.puml
title Figure 3.6 — Nora MedLink Sequence Diagram: AI Summary Generation

actor Patient
participant "Patient Report API" as API
participant "Report AI Pipeline" as Pipeline
participant "BioBERT Entity Service" as BioBERT
participant "Rule Validation Service" as Rules
participant "OpenAI Summary Service" as OpenAI
participant "Summary Self-Check" as SelfCheck
database "PostgreSQL Database" as DB

Patient -> API : Save OCR text or upload report
API -> Pipeline : run(cleanedText, formattedText, structuredData, department)
Pipeline -> BioBERT : extractMedicalEntities(text, fields)
BioBERT --> Pipeline : entities, metadata
Pipeline -> Rules : validateMedicalRules(text, fields, entities)
Rules --> Pipeline : validationStatus, warnings
Pipeline -> OpenAI : generateClinicalSupportSummary(prompt)
alt OpenAI returns valid JSON
  OpenAI --> Pipeline : clinicalSummaryJson
else OpenAI unavailable or invalid
  OpenAI --> Pipeline : error
  Pipeline -> Pipeline : build rule-based fallback summary
end
Pipeline -> SelfCheck : verify summary against OCR evidence
SelfCheck --> Pipeline : passed, confidenceLevel, notes
Pipeline --> API : MedicalAiAnalysis payload
API -> DB : Update PatientReport and insert MedicalAiAnalysis
DB --> API : Saved summary and validation data
API --> Patient : Display summary, warnings and confidence level
@enduml
